cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "haploStack: Haplotype Block Analysis and Stacking Simulation for Genomic Breeding"
version: 0.8.8
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CCS-voidBird/haploStack"
url: "https://github.com/CCS-voidBird/haploStack"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for haplotype block definition, catalogue construction, and
  breeding-cycle simulation (haplotype stacking) in diploid crop species.
  The workflow covers genotype format standardisation, haplotype blocks from a
  user-supplied block map (optionally built locally from LD with HapSelect or
  SelectionTools), haplotype catalogue construction with per-sample local GEBVs,
  and breeding-cycle simulation of haplotype stacking under truncation, optimal
  haplotype and genotype building selection. Designed for the GRDC barley
  haplotype stacking project but applicable to any biparental or multiparental
  breeding programme.
keywords:
  - haplotype blocks
  - genomic selection
  - haplotype stacking
  - plant breeding
  - barley
  - R package
authors:
